<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kanhoji Angre</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1669">1669</a>–<a href="/years/1729">1729</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kanhoji Angre was the commander of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> navy in the early 18th century, based at Kolaba and the sea forts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konkan-coast">Konkan coast</a> such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vijaydurg">Vijaydurg</a>. He seized merchant ships of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">English East India Company</a> and other powers that refused his passes and beat off English and Portuguese attacks on his forts. Europeans called him a pirate, but he made the Marathas a naval power on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>'s west coast.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kanhoji-angre.jpg" alt="Kanhoji Angre" width="320" height="345" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pratish Khedekar · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sarkhel_Kanhoji_Angre_I.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
